**Short Story:**

Gnome warlock Fizzlebang cackled as his succubus, Ladyheart, gracefully dispatched a jungle troll in Stranglethorn Vale. Her seduction ability had proven invaluable - not just for turning enemies into temporary allies, but for gathering information from the pirate crews along the coast. While other warlocks struggled with their bulky voidwalkers, Fizzlebang found Ladyheart's mobility and charm spells made quick work of the zone's elite mobs. Her ability to generate rage through seduction meant he never ran out of mana, and her stunning beauty certainly didn't hurt when negotiating with the Bloodsail Buccaneers. As they headed toward Nesingwary's camp, Fizzlebang mused that his fellow warlocks were missing out on the obvious choice.

**Answer:**

Seduction. The succubus's seduction ability turns enemies into allies and generates significant rage, making them incredibly efficient for solo questing and leveling. This skill also provides unique utility for gathering information and turning tough mobs into temporary allies, which is why experienced warlocks actually prefer succubi despite the voidwalker's tankier reputation. [end of text]


